{"id": "EUVD-2026-96317", "enisaUuid": "7dbfa146-5aa4-35ba-a5f9-28451f9ca3c2", "description": "Pingvin Share X before 1.22.0 contains a rate limit bypass vulnerability that allows unauthenticated remote attackers to evade per-IP throttling because backend/src/main.ts unconditionally trusts proxy headers. Attackers can rotate spoofed X-Forwarded-For values against /api/auth/signIn, /api/auth/signIn/totp, and /api/auth/resetPassword to brute-force passwords and TOTP codes and forge logged client IP addresses.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T13:55:13", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T11:32:31", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/smp46/pingvin-share-x/security/advisories/GHSA-7gx2-g6x2-7mjg", "https://github.com/smp46/pingvin-share-x/commit/25e9cee7fb1c155300b5663fc5fedeea32d20954", "https://github.com/smp46/pingvin-share-x/releases/tag/v1.22.0", "https://github.com/smp46/pingvin-share-x/blob/68ebf191fe1362592ffd5517e662f087e36c10b2/backend/src/main.ts#L57", "https://github.com/smp46/pingvin-share-x", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/pingvin-share-x-before-1.22.0-rate-limit-bypass-via-spoofed-x-forwarded-for"], "aliases": ["GHSA-3chq-cx7h-2cfx", "CVE-2026-108162"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "079c521b-67bb-3669-a867-abdee949b24e", "product": {"name": "pingvin-share-x", "vendor": {"name": "smp46"}}, "product_version": "0 <1.22.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c9d7d9af-441b-3b15-a34d-a2a2b1669f3c", "vendor": {"name": "smp46"}}], "isExploited": false}